Vikram and Betal: The Generous Farmer (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100149

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a farmer who had a good harvest,” said Betal. “He had more food than he needed.”

Instead of keeping everything for himself, he shared his crops with poor people in the village.

Some people asked, “Why are you giving away your food?”

The farmer replied, “Sharing what we have makes everyone happy.”

The next year, when his crops failed, the villagers helped him.

They shared their food with him.

The farmer smiled and said, “Kindness always comes back.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the farmer wise?”

Vikram replied, “He understood the value of sharing and kindness.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Sharing brings kindness in return.
